  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "short": "Hit Enter",
      "title": "Users say the shop feels slow",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "body": "Before you can make something faster, you need to know where the time goes. So let’s follow a single page load.\n\nYou type `shop.example` and press Enter. About a sixth of a second later the page appears. A lot happens in between.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "Every web request is a conversation between machines. Each step costs time, and the costs add up."
      },
      "changes": [],
      "metrics": {},
      "overrides": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "short": "Find address",
      "title": "Find the address (DNS)",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "Networks route by numeric IP address, not by name. So the browser first asks a [[DNS]] resolver: *where is shop.example?*\n\nThe answer — `203.0.113.7` — comes back in about 20 ms.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Answers are cached for a time-to-live (TTL). For the next few minutes, repeat visits skip this step entirely."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ DNS resolver",
        "+ Lookup: 20 ms"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "dns": "20 ms",
        "total": "20 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "short": "Connect",
      "title": "Open a connection",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "Now the browser opens a connection to `203.0.113.7`. A TCP handshake agrees to talk; a TLS handshake sets up encryption. Each needs a [[round trip]] — there and back.\n\nHere a round trip takes 30 ms, so connecting costs 60 ms before a single byte of the page is requested.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "Round-trip time (RTT) is set by distance and the network, not by how fast your server is."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Web server",
        "~ DNS answer cached",
        "+ Handshake: 2 round trips = 60 ms"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "dns": "20 ms",
        "connect": "60 ms",
        "total": "80 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "short": "Request",
      "title": "Send the request",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "Over the open connection the browser sends `GET /products`. The server parses it, checks the session and runs your code.\n\nThat costs one more round trip plus ~10 ms of server work.",
      "changes": [
        "+ Request: 1 round trip + 10 ms server time"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "dns": "20 ms",
        "connect": "60 ms",
        "request": "40 ms",
        "total": "120 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "web": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "short": "Fetch data",
      "title": "The server asks the database",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "The products don’t live in the web server — they live in a [[database]]. The server sends a query and waits for the rows to come back.\n\nWatch a request travel all the way in and the response all the way out.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Keeping the server stateless and the data in a database is what later lets us run many servers. (See Scaling.)"
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Database",
        "+ Query: 15 ms"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "dns": "20 ms",
        "connect": "60 ms",
        "request": "55 ms",
        "total": "135 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "web": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "short": "Response",
      "title": "The response comes home",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "body": "The server turns rows into HTML and sends it back; downloading it takes another 20 ms. The browser renders the page — **155 ms** after you pressed Enter.\n\nThen it notices images and stylesheets in the page and fires off more requests. Reusing the open connection saves them the handshake.",
      "changes": [
        "+ Download: 20 ms",
        "~ Page ready after 155 ms"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "dns": "20 ms",
        "connect": "60 ms",
        "request": "55 ms",
        "download": "20 ms",
        "total": "155 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "dev": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "web": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "q-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "h-2": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "short": "More files",
      "title": "One page, forty more requests",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "The HTML is only the start. It references images, stylesheets, scripts and fonts — about **40 more files** — and the browser fetches them all.\n\nWith old HTTP/1.1 each connection carried one request at a time, so browsers opened ~6 connections and queued the rest. [[HTTP/2]] sends them all at once over the single connection we already opened.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
